# Security

- Never commit secrets.
- Never log passwords.
- Never log authentication tokens.
- Validate external input before use.
- Do not expose raw database errors over HTTP.
- Authentication and authorization are separate concerns.
- Use least privilege for databases and MCP access.
- Never connect Cursor to a production database by default.
- Do not modify production infrastructure or production data unless explicitly instructed.

Local Docker credentials in `.env.example` are development placeholders. They are not production secrets and must not be reused outside local development.
